            <ArticleTitle>Botox for back pain and &quot;regular&quot; versus migraine headaches.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This feature presents information for patients in a question and answer format. It is written to simulate actual questions that many pain patients ask and to provide answers in a context and language that most pain patients will comprehend. Issues addressed in this issue are the use of botulinum toxin to treat back pain and differences between tension-type and migraine headaches.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
